{
 "about": "Every host that non-test source under apps/map lib, app, components, scripts, dataops and ml names, and what the app does with it. Checked by lib/server/hosts.test.ts (map-ci) and scripts/hosts-check.mjs (guard.yml), both through lib/server/hosts.scan.mjs. A new host fails until it is classified here; an entry no code names fails as stale. kind request: the app asks this host for data or images (server or browser), so it carries the publisher and whether it needs a key. kind link: a URL shown or cited (a citation, a terms page, a page a person clicks), not requested; this is a reviewed claim and the check does not prove it. kind identifier: a name that is never dereferenced (an XML namespace, a placeholder). keyless true is a reviewed claim; the only machine check is that no URL literal puts key=, apikey=, token= or the like on such a host (keyParamNote answers that for a host where the parameter is not a credential). keyless false is allowed only for an optional key the user enters in Settings (lib/store/settings.ts API_KEYS); the app works without it, and no key ships in the repo. Not seen: a host built at run time or returned by an upstream, a key sent in a header, hosts a bundled library picks from a token (Cesium ion, the child tiles of Google 3D Tiles), and python or JS outside the scanned directories.",
 "decisionsForCam": [
  "AGENTS.md says one source needs a key today (AISStream). The code has more hosts that take a key the user enters: Google 3D Tiles, ADS-B Exchange via RapidAPI, OpenSky OAuth, AISStream, Windy Webcams, ElevenLabs. All are optional: each is off until a person pastes a key in Settings (AISStream also runs for the snapshot collector if the operator sets AISSTREAM_KEY); no key ships in the repo. pendingCam marks the one AGENTS.md already names. Whether the others stay, go, or are named in AGENTS.md is Cam's call."
 ],
